    "q-61145": {
      "dom_id": "step-q61145",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "A sequence is defined as ${a}_{n}=3n-2$ for $n\\ge 1.$ What is the sum of the third and fourth terms?",
      "worked_solution": "We substitute $n=3$ and $n=4$ into the definition of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & =3(3)-2=7 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =3(4)-2=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the third and fourth terms is\n\n$$\n{a}_{3}+{a}_{4}=7+10=17.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
